# ⚠️  THIS ROOT-LEVEL FILE IS NOT LOADED BY THE BACKEND.
#
# The backend container gets its configuration from backend/.env, which
# docker-compose.yml loads via `env_file: backend/.env`. Creating a .env from
# THIS file and placing it in the project root will NOT set JWT_SECRET (nor any
# other backend variable) — the backend would then crash-loop at startup with
# "JWT_SECRET is not set".
#
# Do this instead:
#
#     cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#     # then edit backend/.env and fill in JWT_SECRET and the rest
#
# backend/.env.example is the single authoritative, complete list of every
# variable the backend consumes (JWT_SECRET, CORS_ORIGINS, COOKIE_SECURE,
# LOG_LEVEL, PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN, TELEGRAM_*, DIGIPAY_*, SMS_*, SMTP_*, …).
#
# A .env file in this project-root directory is read by Docker Compose ONLY for
# ${VARIABLE} interpolation. The only variable docker-compose.yml interpolates
# is CORS_ORIGINS (in its `environment:` block). Never put secrets here.
